      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine when all four tutors (Wanda, Darren, Beatrice, and Chi) will next be together tutoring in the math lab, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of their working intervals. The intervals are 3 days for Darren, 4 days for Wanda, 6 days for Beatrice, and 7 days for Chi.\n\nFirst, we find the prime factorization of each of these numbers:\n- The prime factorization of 3 is \\(3\\).\n- The prime factorization of 4 is \\(2^2\\).\n- The prime factorization of 6 is \\(2 \\times 3\\).\n- The prime factorization of 7 is \\(7\\).\n\nThe LCM is found by taking the highest power of each prime that appears in these factorizations:\n- The highest power of 2 is \\(2^2\\).\n- The highest power of 3 is \\(3\\).\n- The highest power of 7 is \\(7\\).\n\nTherefore, the LCM is:\n\\[\n2^2 \\times 3 \\times 7 = 4 \\times 3 \\times 7 = 84\n\\]\n\nSo, the least common multiple of 3, 4, 6, and 7 is 84. This means that all four tutors will next be together tutoring in the lab in \\(\\boxed{84}\\) school days from today.",
