      "text": "To determine when Wanda, Darren, Beatrice, and Chi will next be together working in the math lab, we need to find the smallest positive integer \\( n \\) such that \\( n \\) is a common multiple of 3, 4, 6, and 7. This is equivalent to finding the least common multiple (LCM) of these numbers.\n\nFirst, we find the prime factorizations of the numbers:\n- The prime factorization of 3 is \\( 3 \\).\n- The prime factorization of 4 is \\( 2^2 \\).\n- The prime factorization of 6 is \\( 2 \\times 3 \\).\n- The prime factorization of 7 is \\( 7 \\).\n\nThe LCM is found by taking the highest power of each prime that appears in these factorizations:\n- The highest power of 2 is \\( 2^2 \\).\n- The highest power of 3 is \\( 3 \\).\n- The highest power of 7 is \\( 7 \\).\n\nTherefore, the LCM is:\n\\[\n2^2 \\times 3 \\times 7 = 4 \\times 3 \\times 7 = 84\n\\]\n\nSo, the next time Wanda, Darren, Beatrice, and Chi will all be together in the math lab is in \\( \\boxed{84} \\) school days from today.",
